{
  "id": "COMPOUND:42544 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "The compound (1S,2S)-1-(4-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenyl)-2-[4-[(2S,3R,4R)-4-[(4-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenyl)methyl]-3-(hydroxymethyl)oxolan-2-yl]-2-methoxyphenoxy]propane-1,3-diol is implicated in the regulation of DNA polymerase iota through multiple pathways. This relationship is supported by the evidence that the compound acts as a target of several bioactive molecules, including 14-deoxy-11,12-dehydroandrographolide, Lychnostatin 1, and 1,2,3,5-tetrahydroxyxanthone, all of which are known to interact with DNA polymerase iota. These findings suggest that the compound may exert its effects through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of the mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 7, which serves as a key intermediate in the signaling cascade leading to DNA polymerase iota activation. The consistent involvement of mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 7 across different targets implies a potential role in the regulation of DNA polymerase iota, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence is robust and consistent across multiple pathways, supporting a plausible biological relationship between the compound and DNA polymerase iota.",
